{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00419",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.73,
      "end_seconds": 6.24,
      "duration_seconds": 5.51,
      "text": "Hi doctor, sorry, the lift was out and I had to take the stairs."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.26,
      "end_seconds": 10.47,
      "duration_seconds": 3.21,
      "text": "That's alright, take a seat. Tell me why you've come."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 11.21,
      "end_seconds": 20.82,
      "duration_seconds": 9.61,
      "text": "Doctor, it's my heart racing. It's getting on my nerves now. I wasn't sure whether to come in at all, to be honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 21.91,
      "end_seconds": 25.27,
      "duration_seconds": 3.36,
      "text": "Is this recent, or has it been a while?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 25.79,
      "end_seconds": 31.37,
      "duration_seconds": 5.58,
      "text": "About... well, four weeks. It's a relief to finally sit down and talk about it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 32.57,
      "end_seconds": 34.25,
      "duration_seconds": 1.68,
      "text": "How often does it happen?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 35.02,
      "end_seconds": 37.55,
      "duration_seconds": 2.53,
      "text": "I'd say a few times a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 37.9,
      "end_seconds": 40.08,
      "duration_seconds": 2.18,
      "text": "Okay, and how severe is it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 40.51,
      "end_seconds": 41.82,
      "duration_seconds": 1.31,
      "text": "Severe, I'd say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 42.36,
      "end_seconds": 43.93,
      "duration_seconds": 1.57,
      "text": "Does anything make it better?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 44.87,
      "end_seconds": 55.43,
      "duration_seconds": 10.56,
      "text": "I get some relief from lying down. I've also been sweating. With sweating, moderate, I'd say. I've also had a fluttering in the chest, for three days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 56.26,
      "end_seconds": 57.98,
      "duration_seconds": 1.72,
      "text": "And how severe is it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 61.56,
      "end_seconds": 62.92,
      "duration_seconds": 1.36,
      "text": "It's moderate, honestly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 64.44,
      "end_seconds": 67.79,
      "duration_seconds": 3.35,
      "text": "I'll try to keep this as efficient as I can."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 68.58,
      "end_seconds": 70.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.21,
      "text": "Thank you, I appreciate it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 71.1,
      "end_seconds": 73.37,
      "duration_seconds": 2.27,
      "text": "Any fainting or weight loss at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 74.95,
      "end_seconds": 78.37,
      "duration_seconds": 3.42,
      "text": "I haven't had fainting or weight loss, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 79.13,
      "end_seconds": 84.04,
      "duration_seconds": 4.91,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any leg swelling, tremor or chest pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 84.99,
      "end_seconds": 86.64,
      "duration_seconds": 1.65,
      "text": "Nothing like that, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 87.96,
      "end_seconds": 91.64,
      "duration_seconds": 3.68,
      "text": "Right, do you have everything you need to get home alright?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 93.23,
      "end_seconds": 107.17,
      "duration_seconds": 13.94,
      "text": "Yes, you know, I've got my transport sorted. It's a bit of a trek, but I'm used to the journey by now, and I brought something to read for the wait."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 108.58,
      "end_seconds": 110.91,
      "duration_seconds": 2.33,
      "text": "Are you on any regular medication?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 111.49,
      "end_seconds": 113.78,
      "duration_seconds": 2.29,
      "text": "No, um, nothing regular."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 115.06,
      "end_seconds": 118.88,
      "duration_seconds": 3.82,
      "text": "Let me make a quick note of that before I forget."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 119.29,
      "end_seconds": 119.99,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 133.39,
      "end_seconds": 138.83,
      "duration_seconds": 5.44,
      "text": "Okay, here we go. Right, do you have any medical conditions, anything you've been treated for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 140.25,
      "end_seconds": 144.4,
      "duration_seconds": 4.15,
      "text": "I have anxiety. I'm hoping you can tell me something definite."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 144.81,
      "end_seconds": 148.95,
      "duration_seconds": 4.14,
      "text": "Sorry, I'm just writing a few notes, bear with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 149.67,
      "end_seconds": 152.02,
      "duration_seconds": 2.35,
      "text": "No problem, take your time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 153.01,
      "end_seconds": 154.94,
      "duration_seconds": 1.93,
      "text": "Any operations in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 155.44,
      "end_seconds": 168.98,
      "duration_seconds": 13.54,
      "text": "Just my thyroid operated on, a long time ago. I looked a few things up online, and that probably didn't help. I thought it would sort itself out, but it hasn't."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 170.21,
      "end_seconds": 173.49,
      "duration_seconds": 3.28,
      "text": "Is it okay if I type while we talk?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 174.29,
      "end_seconds": 177.07,
      "duration_seconds": 2.78,
      "text": "So, yes, of course, go ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 178.25,
      "end_seconds": 180.93,
      "duration_seconds": 2.68,
      "text": "Do you have any known allergies at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 182.49,
      "end_seconds": 183.5,
      "duration_seconds": 1.01,
      "text": "Yes, aspirin."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 184.52,
      "end_seconds": 200.4,
      "duration_seconds": 15.88,
      "text": "Let me explain how I'm thinking about this. When someone has symptoms like these, we first look for the common and treatable causes, and only then for the rarer ones. That's why I'm going step by step rather than ordering everything at once."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 201.79,
      "end_seconds": 203.57,
      "duration_seconds": 1.78,
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 204.94,
      "end_seconds": 210.7,
      "duration_seconds": 5.76,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. Pressure 125 over 80, pulse 112, respiratory rate 19."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 212.11,
      "end_seconds": 228.93,
      "duration_seconds": 16.82,
      "text": "Good, thank you. I'll be straight with you about how this works. Most of what we see in clinic turns out to be manageable, and the history you give me is often more useful than any single test, so thank you for being so detailed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 229.51,
      "end_seconds": 231.63,
      "duration_seconds": 2.12,
      "text": "Thank you, that really helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 234.18,
      "end_seconds": 235.93,
      "duration_seconds": 1.75,
      "text": "Can I examine you now?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 236.64,
      "end_seconds": 237.96,
      "duration_seconds": 1.32,
      "text": "Okay, go ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 239.56,
      "end_seconds": 241.5,
      "duration_seconds": 1.94,
      "text": "Look straight ahead for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 260.35,
      "end_seconds": 263.3,
      "duration_seconds": 2.95,
      "text": "No murmurs and the neck veins aren't distended."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 266.28,
      "end_seconds": 274.68,
      "duration_seconds": 8.4,
      "text": "All done, thank you, please sit down. Good, that's all I need to examine. Let me gather my thoughts and then we'll talk it through together."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 275.35,
      "end_seconds": 279.18,
      "duration_seconds": 3.83,
      "text": "Give me a second, I'm just scrolling back through your chart."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 279.93,
      "end_seconds": 280.69,
      "duration_seconds": 0.76,
      "text": "Of course."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 292.76,
      "end_seconds": 305.97,
      "duration_seconds": 13.21,
      "text": "Right, thanks for waiting. Putting it all together, my working impression is a possible heart rhythm problem like atrial fibrillation. I want to be honest that this is an impression, not a final answer."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 307.53,
      "end_seconds": 311.84,
      "duration_seconds": 4.31,
      "text": "I've been thinking the worst, to be honest. Is it bad?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 313.18,
      "end_seconds": 330.9,
      "duration_seconds": 17.72,
      "text": "It's reasonable to be concerned, but right now a possible heart rhythm problem like atrial fibrillation is my leading thought, not anything worse. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had your heart racing for four weeks, severe, and no tremor or leg swelling."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 332.36,
      "end_seconds": 334.33,
      "duration_seconds": 1.97,
      "text": "Exactly, that's what's been happening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 337.75,
      "end_seconds": 359.17,
      "duration_seconds": 21.42,
      "text": "We should do an ECG for palpitations. The result will help us decide whether anything more is needed. Let's use metoprolol, 25 milligrams, twice a day, until we review. You take it by mouth. It's for palpitations. It's a commonly used medicine and most people tolerate it well. Cut back on tea, coffee and energy drinks, and note the time whenever it happens."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 360.32,
      "end_seconds": 385.27,
      "duration_seconds": 24.95,
      "text": "Try to keep a simple diary of when it happens and what you were doing, and bring it to the next visit. Please take the tablets with food so they don't upset your stomach. Keep an eye out, and if you faint or have chest pain with the racing, call us the same day or go to emergency. Please come and see me after the results are back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 385.95,
      "end_seconds": 386.65,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 387.51,
      "end_seconds": 393.8,
      "duration_seconds": 6.29,
      "text": "Before we finish, can you repeat the plan back to me so I know I haven't been confusing?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 394.73,
      "end_seconds": 402.68,
      "duration_seconds": 7.95,
      "text": "So, I take the metoprolol, 25 milligrams, twice a day and come back after the results are back. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 404.16,
      "end_seconds": 408.77,
      "duration_seconds": 4.61,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Take care, and don't hesitate to call if anything changes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 409.99,
      "end_seconds": 413.12,
      "duration_seconds": 3.13,
      "text": "Well, no, you've explained it well. Thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 414.46,
      "end_seconds": 415.25,
      "duration_seconds": 0.79,
      "text": "Alright, goodbye."
    }
  ]
}